Fix for the pre-existing flake broker::a_sandboxed_jvm_holding_only_the_placeholder
(join_warm = 403 instead of 204). For the integrator; NOT applied on this branch, because
tests/broker.rs and tests/java/BrokerProbe.java belong to the broker work of this round.
Apply after merging with: git apply docs/notes/broker-test-race.patch

Cause: BrokerProbe opens the game connection and asks for the join at once. new Socket()
returns when the kernel has queued the connection at the relay's listener, which can be
before the relay has accepted it, connected to the server and registered it
(gate.opened in egress::relay_game). The fix lets the stand-in game server echo and the
probe wait (at most 15 s) for the echo, which can only come back once the relay splices,
i.e. after the registration. A real client cannot hit the race: it joins only after the
server has answered through the connection.

Verified (fourth engineer, see voice-chat-progress.md section 6.2): with a 1 s delay
injected before gate.opened, the test failed 4 of 4 runs without this patch and passed
4 of 4 with it; without the delay, 40 of 40 runs passed with the patch.

diff --git a/tests/broker.rs b/tests/broker.rs
index 2014cf4..4149860 100644
--- a/tests/broker.rs
+++ b/tests/broker.rs
@@ -508,7 +508,13 @@ async fn a_sandboxed_jvm_holding_only_the_placeholder() {
             std::thread::spawn(move || {
                 let mut stream = stream;
                 let mut buf = [0u8; 64];
-                while matches!(std::io::Read::read(&mut stream, &mut buf), Ok(n) if n > 0) {}
+                // Echoes: an echo can only arrive once the relay has connected and is
+                // splicing, which is after it has registered the game connection.
+                while let Ok(n) = std::io::Read::read(&mut stream, &mut buf) {
+                    if n == 0 || std::io::Write::write_all(&mut stream, &buf[..n]).is_err() {
+                        break;
+                    }
+                }
             });
         }
     });
diff --git a/tests/java/BrokerProbe.java b/tests/java/BrokerProbe.java
index 7fa12c3..796b138 100644
--- a/tests/java/BrokerProbe.java
+++ b/tests/java/BrokerProbe.java
@@ -68,6 +68,14 @@ public final class BrokerProbe {
         System.out.println("join_cold=" + request("POST", "https://sessionserver.mojang.com/session/minecraft/join", null, join));
         try (Socket game = new Socket("127.0.0.1", gamePort)) {
             game.getOutputStream().write(1);
+            // Wait for the server's echo: a real client asks for a join only after the
+            // server has answered through this connection, never right after connecting.
+            // (new Socket returns once the kernel has queued the connection at the relay's
+            // listener; the echo comes back only after the relay has connected to the
+            // server and registered the connection.) Bounded, so that a relay that never
+            // splices ends the probe with an exception instead of a hang.
+            game.setSoTimeout(15000);
+            game.getInputStream().read();
             System.out.println("join_warm=" + request("POST", "https://sessionserver.mojang.com/session/minecraft/join", null, join));
             System.out.println("join_again=" + request("POST", "https://sessionserver.mojang.com/session/minecraft/join", null, join));
         }
